1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,725
<font color="#FFFFFF">How do living systems learn so much from so little,</font>

2
00:00:04,805 --> 00:00:09,030
<font color="#FFFFFF">adapting with sparse data and minimal energy while
artificial deep networks demand massive</font>

3
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:13,335
<font color="#FFFFFF">datasets and constant retraining?</font>

4
00:00:13,415 --> 00:00:17,640
<font color="#FFFFFF">This work by Aisha Belhadi at the Okinawa Institute
of Science and Technology looks to biology for answers.</font>

5
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:21,945
<font color="#FFFFFF">It distills three mechanisms of biological
adaptation metaplasticity, homeostasis,</font>

6
00:00:22,025 --> 00:00:26,250
<font color="#FFFFFF">and inhibition</font>

7
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:30,555
<font color="#FFFFFF">and proposes concrete ways to fold them into the
Hopfield-network self-optimization model,</font>

8
00:00:30,635 --> 00:00:34,860
<font color="#FFFFFF">aiming for deep learning tools that learn the way
living systems do.</font>

9
00:00:35,240 --> 00:00:40,361
<font color="#FFFFFF">A large part of recent AI progress comes from deep
learning paired with big data,</font>

10
00:00:40,441 --> 00:00:43,378
<font color="#FFFFFF">trained by supervised or reinforcement signals.</font>

11
00:00:43,458 --> 00:00:48,579
<font color="#FFFFFF">These systems are powerful, but they behave very
differently from living systems,</font>

12
00:00:48,659 --> 00:00:53,844
<font color="#FFFFFF">which learn, make associations, and adapt using
sparse data, efficient energy use,</font>

13
00:00:53,924 --> 00:00:55,642
<font color="#FFFFFF">and few training iterations.</font>

14
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:59,366
<font color="#FFFFFF">They also forget previous tasks when trained sequentially,</font>

15
00:00:59,446 --> 00:01:02,127
<font color="#FFFFFF">a problem known as catastrophic forgetting.</font>

16
00:01:02,207 --> 00:01:06,749
<font color="#FFFFFF">Hopfield networks, with unsupervised learning and
an associative memory,</font>

17
00:01:06,829 --> 00:01:09,831
<font color="#FFFFFF">offer a more biologically plausible alternative,</font>

18
00:01:09,911 --> 00:01:12,207
<font color="#FFFFFF">but their simplest forms are limited,</font>

19
00:01:12,287 --> 00:01:17,151
<font color="#FFFFFF">storing only about zero point one four times the
number of nodes in patterns,</font>

20
00:01:17,231 --> 00:01:21,260
<font color="#FFFFFF">and rarely exploit the biological mechanisms that
inspired them.</font>

21
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:25,368
<font color="#FFFFFF">To adapt in an uncertain, changing world,</font>

22
00:01:25,448 --> 00:01:29,177
<font color="#FFFFFF">complex systems must integrate new information
while maintaining stability.</font>

23
00:01:29,257 --> 00:01:32,985
<font color="#FFFFFF">Too much destabilization prevents consistent learning;</font>

24
00:01:33,065 --> 00:01:36,793
<font color="#FFFFFF">too much reliance on past memory locks in outdated
patterns.</font>

25
00:01:36,873 --> 00:01:40,602
<font color="#FFFFFF">Biology solves this with an interplay of mechanisms</font>

26
00:01:40,682 --> 00:01:44,410
<font color="#FFFFFF">metaplasticity that tunes how much synapses change,</font>

27
00:01:44,490 --> 00:01:48,218
<font color="#FFFFFF">homeostasis that regulates the system around a set
point, inhibition,</font>

28
00:01:48,298 --> 00:01:52,027
<font color="#FFFFFF">and resets that enable forgetting.</font>

29
00:01:52,107 --> 00:01:55,835
<font color="#FFFFFF">The self-optimization model is a Hopfield network
with Hebbian learning and periodic resets</font>

30
00:01:55,915 --> 00:01:59,643
<font color="#FFFFFF">that already builds a memory of visited attractors
and enlarges the basin of the global</font>

31
00:01:59,723 --> 00:02:03,452
<font color="#FFFFFF">energy minimum,</font>

32
00:02:03,532 --> 00:02:07,260
<font color="#FFFFFF">making it a promising candidate to be enriched with
more of these biological features.</font>

33
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:11,492
<font color="#FFFFFF">This work makes two linked contributions.</font>

34
00:02:11,572 --> 00:02:15,424
<font color="#FFFFFF">First, it distills key mechanisms of adaptation in
biological systems,</font>

35
00:02:15,504 --> 00:02:19,355
<font color="#FFFFFF">with a special focus on metaplasticity and
homeostatic regulation,</font>

36
00:02:19,435 --> 00:02:23,287
<font color="#FFFFFF">plus inhibition and forgetting.</font>

37
00:02:23,367 --> 00:02:27,219
<font color="#FFFFFF">Second,</font>

38
00:02:27,299 --> 00:02:31,151
<font color="#FFFFFF">it proposes concrete avenues to incorporate these
features into the self-optimization</font>

39
00:02:31,231 --> 00:02:35,083
<font color="#FFFFFF">model and Hopfield networks more broadly</font>

40
00:02:35,163 --> 00:02:39,015
<font color="#FFFFFF">by making the learning rate adaptive with respect
to synaptic weights or the energy landscape,</font>

41
00:02:39,095 --> 00:02:42,946
<font color="#FFFFFF">by enhancing modular structure, and by changing the
activation rule.</font>

42
00:02:43,026 --> 00:02:46,878
<font color="#FFFFFF">The aim is deep learning tools that recapitulate
the advantages of biological systems</font>

43
00:02:46,958 --> 00:02:50,810
<font color="#FFFFFF">and can plausibly model living and adaptive systems
across levels of complexity.</font>

44
00:02:51,190 --> 00:02:56,663
<font color="#FFFFFF">The core idea is to raise the network's degrees of
freedom without adding new parameters,</font>

45
00:02:56,743 --> 00:03:00,468
<font color="#FFFFFF">by letting existing components do more work, as
biology does.</font>

46
00:03:00,548 --> 00:03:02,028
<font color="#FFFFFF">For local metaplasticity,</font>

47
00:03:02,108 --> 00:03:07,830
<font color="#FFFFFF">the learning rate alpha is no longer a user-defined
constant but a function of the connection</font>

48
00:03:07,910 --> 00:03:09,390
<font color="#FFFFFF">weight between two nodes,</font>

49
00:03:09,470 --> 00:03:14,880
<font color="#FFFFFF">so the Hebbian update becomes weight-dependent: the
change in a weight equals a function</font>

50
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:18,374
<font color="#FFFFFF">of that weight times the product of the two node states.</font>

51
00:03:18,454 --> 00:03:23,802
<font color="#FFFFFF">This can potentiate co-activated synapses faster
and depress opposing ones more slowly.</font>

52
00:03:23,882 --> 00:03:25,861
<font color="#FFFFFF">For network-level metaplasticity,</font>

53
00:03:25,941 --> 00:03:29,604
<font color="#FFFFFF">alpha is instead tied to the change in the
network's energy,</font>

54
00:03:29,684 --> 00:03:35,281
<font color="#FFFFFF">so learning slows in shallow parts of the energy
landscape and speeds up on steeper slopes,</font>

55
00:03:35,361 --> 00:03:36,966
<font color="#FFFFFF">helping avoid local minima.</font>

56
00:03:37,046 --> 00:03:40,959
<font color="#FFFFFF">Homeostasis is approximated by oscillatory
activation functions,</font>

57
00:03:41,039 --> 00:03:46,262
<font color="#FFFFFF">such as trigonometric ones, and adaptivity is
further supported by modular structure,</font>

58
00:03:46,342 --> 00:03:52,313
<font color="#FFFFFF">where modules that consistently strengthen their
internal connections receive an automatic boost,</font>

59
00:03:52,393 --> 00:03:55,620
<font color="#FFFFFF">and inter-module inhibition regulates overall energy.</font>

60
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:00,887
<font color="#FFFFFF">This paper is a conceptual and position piece
rather than an empirical study,</font>

61
00:04:00,967 --> 00:04:04,306
<font color="#FFFFFF">so it does not introduce a dataset or run benchmarks.</font>

62
00:04:04,386 --> 00:04:09,595
<font color="#FFFFFF">Instead, it builds on existing computational work
with the self-optimization model</font>

63
00:04:09,675 --> 00:04:15,659
<font color="#FFFFFF">including a model of the C. elegans connectome that
used inhibitory inter-cluster connections,</font>

64
00:04:15,739 --> 00:04:19,723
<font color="#FFFFFF">and SO models that solve combinatorial
satisfiability problems.</font>

65
00:04:19,803 --> 00:04:25,400
<font color="#FFFFFF">These prior systems define the setting in which the
proposed biological mechanisms would</font>

66
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,980
<font color="#FFFFFF">eventually be implemented and evaluated.</font>

67
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,373
<font color="#FFFFFF">Because this is a proposal paper,</font>

68
00:04:30,453 --> 00:04:33,670
<font color="#FFFFFF">its main result is conceptual rather than numerical.</font>

69
00:04:33,750 --> 00:04:38,997
<font color="#FFFFFF">It delivers a unified framework showing how
metaplasticity, homeostasis, inhibition,</font>

70
00:04:39,077 --> 00:04:44,071
<font color="#FFFFFF">and forgetting can each map onto specific changes
in the self-optimization model</font>

71
00:04:44,151 --> 00:04:47,495
<font color="#FFFFFF">an adaptive learning rate driven by weights or energy,</font>

72
00:04:47,575 --> 00:04:52,188
<font color="#FFFFFF">oscillatory activation functions, and adaptive
modularity with inhibition.</font>

73
00:04:52,268 --> 00:04:57,642
<font color="#FFFFFF">The unifying insight is that constraints and
degrees of freedom are not in opposition:</font>

74
00:04:57,722 --> 00:05:01,510
<font color="#FFFFFF">the network architecture provides the constraining
framework,</font>

75
00:05:01,590 --> 00:05:06,774
<font color="#FFFFFF">and within it, higher degrees of freedom can expand
the space of adaptive behavior.</font>

76
00:05:06,854 --> 00:05:11,720
<font color="#FFFFFF">Without those constraints, the added freedom would
simply collapse into noise.</font>

77
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:16,695
<font color="#FFFFFF">There are no ablation experiments in this work,
since no model is trained.</font>

78
00:05:16,775 --> 00:05:18,211
<font color="#FFFFFF">The paper does, however,</font>

79
00:05:18,291 --> 00:05:22,444
<font color="#FFFFFF">sketch the variations that a future empirical study
should compare.</font>

80
00:05:22,524 --> 00:05:29,204
<font color="#FFFFFF">These include different forms of the function that
links the learning rate to weights or to energy changes,</font>

81
00:05:29,284 --> 00:05:33,817
<font color="#FFFFFF">ranging from simple linear approximations to more
complex nonlinear ones,</font>

82
00:05:33,897 --> 00:05:38,365
<font color="#FFFFFF">and different activation functions such as sigmoid,
Heaviside threshold,</font>

83
00:05:38,445 --> 00:05:40,134
<font color="#FFFFFF">and trigonometric functions.</font>

84
00:05:40,214 --> 00:05:45,568
<font color="#FFFFFF">The author suggests these variations could
reproduce different normal and pathological</font>

85
00:05:45,648 --> 00:05:48,032
<font color="#FFFFFF">behavioral modes in biological systems,</font>

86
00:05:48,112 --> 00:05:52,770
<font color="#FFFFFF">and are worth exploring systematically once the
mechanisms are implemented.</font>

87
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:58,355
<font color="#FFFFFF">The one quantitative anchor in this paper is the
classic capacity limit of a standard</font>

88
00:05:58,435 --> 00:06:03,764
<font color="#FFFFFF">Hopfield network: it can reliably store only about
zero point one four times the number</font>

89
00:06:03,844 --> 00:06:06,998
<font color="#FFFFFF">of nodes in the network in distinct memory patterns.</font>

90
00:06:07,078 --> 00:06:13,651
<font color="#FFFFFF">This ceiling is a key reason the paper looks to
biological mechanisms to extend the network's capabilities.</font>

91
00:06:13,731 --> 00:06:17,443
<font color="#FFFFFF">Beyond that figure, the work reports no
experimental numbers,</font>

92
00:06:17,523 --> 00:06:22,355
<font color="#FFFFFF">because it is a conceptual proposal that
synthesizes ideas across neuroscience,</font>

93
00:06:22,435 --> 00:06:26,770
<font color="#FFFFFF">molecular biology, and machine learning rather than
measuring a system.</font>

94
00:06:27,150 --> 00:06:30,963
<font color="#FFFFFF">The takeaway is that the mechanisms biology uses to
adapt metaplasticity,</font>

95
00:06:31,043 --> 00:06:34,855
<font color="#FFFFFF">homeostasis, and inhibition</font>

96
00:06:34,935 --> 00:06:38,748
<font color="#FFFFFF">can be translated into machine learning by
adjusting the learning rate according to synaptic</font>

97
00:06:38,828 --> 00:06:42,641
<font color="#FFFFFF">weights or the system's energy,</font>

98
00:06:42,721 --> 00:06:46,534
<font color="#FFFFFF">by enhancing modular structure,</font>

99
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:50,426
<font color="#FFFFFF">and by modifying the activation rule of a
Hopfield-network self-optimization model.</font>

100
00:06:50,506 --> 00:06:54,319
<font color="#FFFFFF">Doing so could yield associative-memory systems
capable of complex adaptive learning from sparse data,</font>

101
00:06:54,399 --> 00:06:58,212
<font color="#FFFFFF">closer to how living systems continually adjust and
thrive.</font>

102
00:06:58,292 --> 00:07:02,105
<font color="#FFFFFF">The broader message is that constraints and
flexibility work together: the right constraints</font>

103
00:07:02,185 --> 00:07:05,997
<font color="#FFFFFF">let increased degrees of freedom open up new
adaptive possibilities instead of collapsing</font>

104
00:07:06,077 --> 00:07:09,890
<font color="#FFFFFF">into noise.</font>
